    "abstract": "Parts figure for the forward cargo door surround, covering the fitting kit, the inboard frame sub-assembly, the aft spar cap and the fastener sets, with the pre and post protection standard split on the washer set.",
    "sections": {
      "purpose": "This figure identifies the structural items of the forward cargo door surround and the fastener sets used to join them, on both sides of the aircraft, and separates the fastener sets by the protective scheme they belong to.",
      "figure_note": "Sheet 1 shows the left-hand installation looking outboard; the right-hand installation is a mirror image and is not drawn. Sheet 2 shows the fastener detail at the frame foot. Item 40 and item 40A are alternates and must not be mixed on one door surround: item 40 is the chromate-free washer set introduced with the protection standard change and item 40A is the earlier cadmium-plated set. The nomenclature of every washer position now names its protective scheme, because three of the four positions read identically on the shelf. CAUTION: DO NOT ORDER A FASTENER SET BY DESCRIPTION. TWO ORDERS IN THE LAST YEAR WERE FILLED WITH CADMIUM PLATED WASHERS ON A CHROMATE-FREE SURROUND, WHICH DEFEATS THE PROTECTION AT THE FAYING SURFACE. Quantities on sheet 2 are for one door surround, both sides."
    },
